---
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
import Nav from "../../components/Nav.astro";
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";

const title = "Case Study: Agent-fleet — Harness Dreams";
const description =
  "A Harness Dreams case study showing how repeated re-asks affect Alignment, Code Flow, and an advice-only coach card.";
---

<SiteLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <Nav />
  <main id="main">
    <article class="article-page">
      <header class="article-hero">
        <div class="container section-narrow">
          <span class="eyebrow">Case study</span>
          <h1>Agent-fleet revealed an alignment drag.</h1>
          <p class="lead">
            A small missing hint created repeated friction. Harness Dreams made
            the day readable: the Dream Score dipped, Code Flow marked the rough
            patch, and the coach suggested what to try next.
          </p>
        </div>
      </header>

      <div class="container article-grid">
        <aside class="article-aside card">
          <img
            src="/story-standing-desk.png"
            alt=""
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            class="aside-image"
          />
          <span class="mono">Result</span>
          <strong>Alignment 64 → 81 target</strong>
          <p>Suggested habit: start that project with the validation command.</p>
        </aside>

        <div class="article-body">
          <h2>The signal</h2>
          <p>
            In several sessions, the agent guessed the validation command,
            failed, and needed the user to redirect it. The raw mistake was
            small. The repeated shape was the important part.
          </p>

          <h2>The tracker view</h2>
          <p>
            The re-asks lowered Alignment, the tool failures touched
            Effectiveness, and Code Flow showed the spiral as a short rapid
            exchange block. The finding was not a vibe; it was visible in three
            places.
          </p>

          <h2>The coach card</h2>
          <p>
            The card suggested starting this repo with the exact validation
            command or copying a project note manually. It did not edit project
            files. The next days simply show whether the Alignment component
            recovers.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</SiteLayout>
